 `.rlmedia` contains every referenced still and retained generic original plus exact owner metadata. It excludes audio-only files, player profiles, saved flights and installed pack payloads. It is an originals backup, not complete game-data backup by itself. Use the game's separate backup/transfer workflow and `.rlsound` alongside it where needed. Imported removed-pack owners retain provenance/history without installing content or granting an earned picture. See [binary bundle validation and bounds](media-bundle.md).
 
+## Shared reading preferences
+
+The standalone page loads the existing `tool-display-entry.mjs` independently of the media application. It applies the game's shared Standard/Large text, Theme/Plain font and reduced-effects preferences before **Open local media**, without opening the media database or saving a preference. The existing Field Kit tokens make Standard controls 16 px and Large controls 20 px; the page does not create a second settings store or another text-size selector.
+
+Shared preference and system-motion updates change only the document's reading attributes. The current editor, selected file, unsaved text, preview, focus and saved media stay intact. A cached-page return refreshes missed preference changes; the media host's existing departure policy still closes its panel, and reading restoration never reopens it. Terminal departure removes subscriptions and cancels pending display repair.
+
+The actual-entry/host regression covers saved preferences before database access, updates with a real unsaved picture preview, cached return and stale callbacks after disposal. It uses modeled DOM/history events and does not establish native font metrics, focus-outline clearance or physical-device behavior. In native verification, choose Large or Plain in the same-origin game Settings, enter **Workshop → Pictures & stories**, and verify actual control font size and file-picker clearance in portrait and short landscape. Preserve the picker fix's separate source identity when combining these changes.
+
+Maintainer prompt: “Reuse the independent shared tool-display entry for Still Media. Verify startup and live preference updates without media access or preference writes. While an original is selected and previewed, preserve its exact bytes, draft metadata, preview ownership, saved generation and current focus. Test cached return and terminal callbacks; then measure Standard/Large and Theme/Plain in the actual browser. Do not interpret an unchanged 16 px control as a Large-text pass.”
+
 ## Bounds and remaining gates
 
 Limits stay at 4 MiB per still, 8,192 pixels per side and 16 megapixels for source images; an assigned poster must be at most 1,920 × 1,080. Shared committed-plus-staging storage remains 256 MiB; rich metadata including owners 2 MiB; image records 512; retained presentation revisions 256. Append-only history consumes these limits. Reads verify all referenced originals sequentially and are cancellable, without a per-file progress meter yet.
